  "name": "ANCA ANTI NEUTROPHIL CYTOPLASMIC ANTIBODIES BY IFA",
  "code": "2664",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9535%; height: 344.792px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 26.7009%;\"><col style=\"width: 40.09%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3954%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.7083px;\">\n<td><strong>Pattern&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Type of Antibody / Antigenic determinants</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Disease Associations</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 131.625px;\">\n<td>pANCA&nbsp;</td>\n<td>MPO, Elastase, Cathepsin G, Lactoferrin, Lysozyme, catalase,<br>Others</td>\n<td>MPO &ndash; Microscopic Polyangitis (Generally), Wegener&rsquo;s<br>Granulomatisis (less commonly), Drug Induced<br>SLE/Vasculitis, Churg Strauss Syndrome</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 112.042px;\">\n<td>cANCA</td>\n<td>PR3, BPI, Cathepsin G, Others</td>\n<td>PR3 &ndash; Wegener&rsquo;s Granulomatosis (Generally), Churg<br>Strauss Syndrome, Microscopic Polyangitis (less<br>commonly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.7083px;\">\n<td>Other Atypical ANCA&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Lactoferrin, Cathepsin G?</td>\n<td>Ulcerative Colitis, SLE, chronic infections, Drug Induced<br>Vasculitis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.7083px;\">\n<td>ANA interference &ndash; Cannot<br>report ANCA</td>\n<td>Anti Nuclear Antibodies</td>\n<td>Connective Tissue Diseases, Autoimmune Hepatitis</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>COMMENTS:</strong><br>-ANCA by IIF using ANCA-L Slides (Immunoconcepts, USA) is a special substrate slide containing Human neutrophils with lymphocytes stabilized and fixed directly on test wells. ---The inclusion<br>of lymphocytes allows detection of ANA interference commonly seen on standard ethanol fixed ANCA slides.<br>-The ANCA-L is able to pickup such an interference using Lymphocytes. A PR3 and MPO ANCA tests are recommended on all ANA interference reported ANCA results. ANCA results should only<br>be interpreted by the clinician in light of patient&rsquo;s clinical information. MPO/PR3 ANCA tests are strongly recommended for ANCA positive patients, and are ideally recommended to be<br>performed on all ANCA requested samples. The decision on treatment should not be based solely on the ANCA results.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
